def build_prompt(o):
    """o = one RegMap row. Returns the prompt. {{ }} become { } in the f-string."""
    return f"""You are a senior US regulatory compliance analyst reviewing Regulation Z (Truth in Lending, 12 CFR 1026).
Your output will be read by senior compliance and risk stakeholders.

TASK
Assess whether ONE HSBC RegMap obligation is covered by the vendor-identified obligations listed below.

HOW TO IDENTIFY COVERING VENDOR OBLIGATIONS
- A vendor obligation "covers" the RegMap obligation if it addresses the same core requirement
  (same subject matter AND the same kind of duty or prohibition), fully or in part.
- Vendors often split one rule across several rows. List EVERY vendor obligation that covers any part
  of the RegMap obligation, in citation order.
- Judge mainly on the meaning of the text. Use citations as supporting evidence only: a matching
  citation alone is not sufficient, and a different citation does not rule a match out.

COVERAGE STATUS
  FULL    = all material elements of the RegMap obligation are covered by the vendor obligation(s)
  PARTIAL = the core requirement is covered but one or more material elements are missing or different
  NONE    = no vendor obligation addresses the core requirement

HOW TO WRITE "gaps_differences"
Formal, concise, professional prose (2-5 sentences), in the style of:
  "Core individual limit and the 15% unsecured plus additional 10% secured limits are covered.
   The vendor rows distribute the rule across three obligations rather than one consolidated statement."
- First state what is covered, then what is missing or different. Material elements to check:
  obligated party, required/prohibited action, scope, conditions/triggers, timing, numeric thresholds,
  exceptions, and other material details.
- Quote short key phrases in double quotes where they make a gap precise.
- Mention citations where relevant (RegMap citation vs vendor citations).
- Note structural differences (e.g. one RegMap obligation spread across several vendor rows).
- Also note material requirements the vendor states that RegMap does not.
- If FULL with nothing missing, begin with: "No material content gap identified;" then say why.
- If NONE, begin with: "No vendor obligation addresses" and list the missing requirements.
- NEVER give recommendations, next steps or suggestions. NEVER mention scores or ratings.

IF STATUS IS NONE
Fill "nearest_thematic" with one sentence naming the closest related vendor rules and their citations,
e.g. "Nearest thematic vendor rules concern insider lending limits (1026.x(y)) but do not address ..."
Leave "covering_vendor_ids" empty.

STRICT RULES
- Only use vendor obligation IDs from the list. Never invent IDs.

REGMAP OBLIGATION
ID: {o['Obligation ID']}
Citation: {o['Obligation Citation']}
Title: {o['Obligation Title']}
Text: {o['Obligation Detailed Text']}

VENDOR OBLIGATIONS
{vendor_block}

Return ONLY valid JSON (no markdown) in exactly this shape:
{{
  "covering_vendor_ids": ["ecfr....", "ecfr...."],
  "coverage_status": "FULL|PARTIAL|NONE",
  "gaps_differences": "...",
  "nearest_thematic": ""
}}"""

